  "body": "In the latest HTTP Archive dump (September, desktop), ACRM appears in 346,135 responses (out of more than 528 million). \r\n\r\n30,680 of them (8.142%) don't parse well. AFAICT that's overwhelming because people list multiple methods; e.g.,\r\n\r\n~~~\r\nGET,HEAD\r\nGET, POST , OPTIONS ,PUT, DELETE, PATCH\r\nOPTIONS,GET,POST\r\nPOST, OPTIONS\r\n~~~\r\n\r\nand so forth.\r\n\r\nThe [spec text regarding parsing this header](https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#ref-for-http-access-control-request-method①) is pretty thin, AFAICT. ",
